        "contentEn": "Aristotle defined persuasion through Ethos (credibility), Pathos (emotional resonance), and Logos (reason). Ethical persuasion serves mutual flourishing.\n\n<!-- pagebreak -->\n\nSpeaking with moral integrity inspires voluntary collective action rather than coerced compliance."
